<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yi Sun-sin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1598">1598</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Admiral Yi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yi Sun-sin was a Korean admiral who led Joseon's navy against the Japanese invasions of 1592 to 1598. Using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turtle-ship">turtle ships</a> and panokseon warships, he won victories such as Hansan Island in 1592 and Myeongnyang in 1597 that cut Japanese supply lines. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-noryang">Battle of Noryang</a> in 1598 and is honoured as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>'s greatest national hero.</p></div>
